{
  "_comment": [
    "BRD-010: the checked-in request plan for the pinned PubChem snapshot.",
    "tools/fetch-pubchem-snapshot.py turns this into raw/snapshot.json, which is",
    "what every test reads. Regenerating the snapshot is a reviewable diff, never",
    "an implicit refresh: the manifest pins the SHA-256 and quarantine-review diff",
    "shows what moved.",
    "",
    "'class' records why a seed is in the fixture; it is documentation for the",
    "reviewer and is never used as data by the adapter.",
    "",
    "Every seed is resolved by name, not by CID, on purpose: name resolution is",
    "itself one of the hazards BRD-010 must report (a mixture name that PubChem",
    "answers with a single pure-compound record, or with a genuine multi-component",
    "record). The CIDs the names resolved to on the retrieval date are pinned in",
    "raw/snapshot.json."
  ],
